27j0|n|One who visits; one who comes or goes to see another, as in civility or friendship. ; A superior, or a person lawfully appointed for the purpose, who makes formal visits of inspection to a corporation or an institution. See Visit, v. t., 2, and Visitation, n., 2.	a:tu5,60,6~tu5,60,6	n:q0p,61,4;1xfu,50,3~q0p,61,4;1xfu,50,3	N:27hk,75,4;bgy,73,4;1xl0,56,2~27hk,75,4;bgy,73,4;1xl0,56,2
27j8|n|A view; especially, a view through or between intervening objects, as trees; a view or prospect through an avenue, or the like; hence, the trees or other objects that form the avenue.	N:27qg,125,2~27qg,125,2
